<p>When applying layout-printing to documents containing a mixture of landscape 
 and portrait pages, you can specify whether to print document pages whose 
 orientation differs from the paper orientation rotated by 90 degrees or 
 reduced in size without being rotated.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="orientation" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Printout Result:</span></p>
<p>Specify a printout result when you apply layout-printing to documents 
 containing a mixture of landscape and portrait pages.</p>
<p aria-level="4" class="T3" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Rotate to same orientation as original</span></p>
<p class="Normal-indent">Document pages whose orientation differs from the 
 paper orientation are not changed, but rotated to a naturally readable 
 direction.</p>
<p aria-level="4" class="T3" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Reduce without Rotation</span></p>
<p class="Normal-indent">Document pages whose orientation differs from the 
 paper orientation are not rotated, but reduced so they can be printed 
 in the same direction.</p>
<p aria-level="4" class="T3" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Page Break</span></p>
<p class="Normal-indent">Creates blank pages so document pages of different 
 orientation are not included.</p>
<p class="Note-indent">Note:</p>
<ul>
<li><p class="Normal-indent">This setting 
 is automatically selected when an item other than <span class="Term-Soft">Printer 
 Defaults</span> is selected in the <span class="Term-Soft">Rotate Mixed 
 Original Orientation</span> dialog box opened from the <span class="Term-Soft">Output 
 Settings</span> menu.</p></li>
</ul>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="ok" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">OK</span></p>
<p>Saves the changes and closes the dialog box.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="cancel" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Cancel</span></p>
<p>Closes the dialog box without saving any changes.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="default" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Restore Defaults</span></p>
<p>Restores the settings on this dialog box to the default settings.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="help" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Help</span></p>
<p>Displays Help for the dialog box opened.</p>
